.TH MORIARTTY 1 "2026-10-21" "Moriartty 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moriartty \- private-by-default terminal emulator inspired by PuTTY's pterm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moriartty
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-e\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moriartty
opens a terminal window running your shell. It keeps PuTTY's habits:
selecting text copies it (to the PRIMARY selection), the right mouse button
pastes, and the settings follow PuTTY's configuration tree.
.PP
Ctrl+Right-click inside the terminal opens the menu (Copy, Paste, Find,
New Tab, New Window, Settings, Event Log, ...).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-load " name"
Use the saved session (settings profile)
.I name
instead of Default Settings.
.TP
.B \-config
Open the settings window first.
.TP
.BI \-title " text\fR, " \-T " text"
Window title.
.TP
.BI \-geometry " columns" x rows
Window size in characters, for example 120x40.
.TP
.BI \-dir " directory\fR, " \-\-working\-directory " directory"
Start in
.IR directory .
.TP
.B \-hold
Keep the window open after the program exits.
.TP
.B \-ls
Run the shell as a login shell.
.TP
.BI \-log " file"
Log all session output to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-e " command " \fR[\fIargs\fR...]
Run
.I command
instead of the shell. It is started directly, not through a shell, and
must be the last option.
.TP
.BR \-help ", " \-version
Show usage or the version, and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Shift+C ", " Ctrl+Insert
Copy to the clipboard.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Shift+V ", " Shift+Insert
Paste from the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+F
Find in scrollback.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+= ", " Ctrl+\- ", " Ctrl+0
Zoom in, out, back to normal.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Shift+T ", " Ctrl+Shift+W
New tab, close tab.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+PgUp ", " Ctrl+PgDn ", " Alt+1 ... Alt+9
Switch tabs (with two or more tabs).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
New window.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Settings.
.TP
.B Ctrl+click
Open the http(s) link under the pointer.
.SH SECURITY
Pasted text is stripped of escape sequences and other control characters,
and pastes of several lines, or with invisible or direction-changing
characters, ask first. Programs cannot write to the clipboard or read the
window title. Only http and https links can be opened, never automatically.
Settings and log files are created private (mode 0600) and symlinks are
refused. See
.I /usr/share/doc/moriartty/README.md
for the full list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MORIARTTY_DEBUG
If set, diagnostics are written to standard error.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where settings are kept (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/moriartty/sessions/
Saved sessions, one TOML file each.
.I Default Settings.toml
applies to every new window.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pterm (1),
.BR putty (1)
